[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) said one issue and one fix. Its reports show three problems. The
subjects match, so the [subject rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) merged them, but the bodies differ.
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October, and all three tickets are now closed.

<Callout kind="warn">
Watch for one-day moves. They closed with the parser fix, but they point at time zones, which that fix does not change. If they come back, reopen their ticket.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the tenant writes the day first, and the shared parser reads every date month
  first, so day and month swap. It happens in the app, in email and in booking-v2 forms.
- **`hint`**: the tenant runs booking-v3. Its form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so
  people type the month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. Day and
  month swap here too, but the parser fix does not touch it: the hint is the bug.
- **`one-day move`**: day and month stay in place, and the date moves by one day. One report
  shows a different day in Lisbon and Toronto for the same meeting, one has an invite that
  arrived before its booking, and one says only June is off. That points at time zones or
  daylight saving, not at date order. The desk saw these
  (`desk-notes.json`) and files them under `parser` by tenant, so they count there too.

Do not trust the intake tag for this. It is guessed from the reporter's browser, and
it disagrees with the tenant on many of these reports.

## Where each problem stands

Engineering update, 5 October, when #4471 closed:

| problem | result | ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` | closed, completed |
| `hint` | won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired | closed, not planned |
| `one-day move` | not in the update; closed with `parser`, where the desk files these reports | closed, duplicate of #1; reopen if they come back |

## What to do

1. Watch new reports for a date that moves by one day. If one comes in, reopen the `one-day move` ticket.
2. Merge on cause, not on subject: [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)
   needs a new record that replaces it.

